# Generated artefacts under output/.
#
# The figure + table deliverables (output/figures/**, output/tables/**) and the
# numbers lookup (output/results/_numbers.json) ARE committed, so the published
# figures and tables can be browsed on GitHub without installing R or running
# the pipeline. The fitted-model objects (output/results/*.rds) and the JSONL
# parse cache (output/results/_data/) are large and fully derivable from
# data/ + code/, so they are not tracked.
output/results/*.rds
output/results/_data/

# Re-identification key: must NEVER appear in the public repo. It only exists
# in the private repo, but this guard keeps it out of the public tree too.
.redact_id_map.csv

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store

# Python: local virtualenv + bytecode caches (e.g. for the elite_debater
# annotation step); never commit them.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# R session / project files
.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj
.lintr

# Stray default-device output R writes when a plot is drawn with no explicit
# device open (guarded against in code, ignored here as a safety net).
Rplots.pdf

# renv: track the lockfile, ignore the local library
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/cellar/
renv/lock/
renv/python/
renv/staging/
.Rprofile.local
